\section{Overview}

This test harness validates our Z80 implementation against the SingleStepTests/z80
test suite. Each JSON file contains 1000 randomized test cases for a single opcode.
For each test case, the harness:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Sets up a flat 64~KB memory with the test's initial RAM contents
\item Loads the test's initial register state into the Z80
\item Executes exactly one instruction
\item Compares all registers and RAM against the expected final state
\end{enumerate}

The test uses a flat memory model (not the Berzerk memory map) because the
tests need arbitrary read/write access to the full 64~KB address space.

